      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"lagerlof-gosta-berlings-saga-9af4d5260c8d49d8\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"The imagined question “Can you believe that I have loved you despite everything?” presents the speaker’s enduring past love as true and asks the dying addressee to recognize it. Its principal force is therefore truth-conditional avowal. It makes no relational undertaking, and the emotional pressure to speak does not establish an independently expressive/reflexive core force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The generic pronoun “man” and quoted first person allow the speech to voice what each cavalier, or the group collectively, wishes to tell the major’s wife; this does not materially affect the T/P/E classification.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"imagined\",\"description\":\"An unspoken, narrator-formulated speech that the cavaliers wish they could address to the dying major’s wife; it is presented in direct quotation but cannot reach her.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Facing the major’s wife’s imminent death, the cavaliers long to secure forgiveness and assure her that their harmful conduct did not negate their love. The perfect form makes the love retrospective and enduring, while “despite everything” acknowledges the conflict between that love and the sorrow they caused. The surrounding urgency, gratitude, and remorse intensify the avowal but do not turn it into a commitment or reflex-like discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“kan du förlåta? Kan du tro, att jag har älskat dig trots allt?” (“can you forgive? Can you believe that I have loved you despite everything?”)\",\"supports\":\"The embedded proposition explicitly presents enduring love as true, strongly supporting T; its interrogative framing seeks belief rather than undertaking a commitment.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Hur kunde det dock bli så, att jag skulle vålla dig så mycken sorg, medan vi vandrade här tillsammans?”\",\"supports\":\"The imagined speaker contrasts professed love with having caused sorrow, framing the avowal as remorseful explanation and relational repair rather than a promise.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Detta ville man säga … Men majorskan låg i brinnande feber, och kavaljerernas röst kunde inte nå henne.”\",\"supports\":\"The passage explicitly marks the quoted speech as wished-for but unrealized because the cavaliers cannot reach the dying woman, supporting imagined status.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Orden trängas på tungan” (“The words crowd upon one’s tongue”).\",\"supports\":\"This supplies emotional urgency and pressure to speak, but not enough independent evidence that the love clause functions as reflexive discharge rather than an urgent avowal.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is identified as affirmative Swedish perfect “jag har älskat dig.”\",\"supports\":\"The perfect construction supports a retrospective avowal of love extending across the shared past.\",\"confidence\":0.98}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. Remorse, urgency, imagined delivery, and the desire for forgiveness are adequately treated as contextual framing; no important aspect of core force falls outside T/P/E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
